        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: сорок",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сорок (sórok) — \"forty\". The odd one out: not built from четыре."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сорок (sórok) — origin disputed. Old Russian sorokŭ was also \"a bundle of forty sable pelts\". Vasmer finds difficulties with Greek (te)ssarákonta, \"forty\", and probably links it with сорочка, \"shirt\", after Old Norse serkr, \"a shirt; a bundle of furs\"; Trubachev thinks a Turkic source, like Turkish kırk, \"forty\", possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
