          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "девяносто (devyanósto) is found only in East Slavic, from 1398 on; other Slavic languages say \"nine tens\". Vasmer thinks it probably comes from an old devęno-desętŭ, \"the ninth ten\", like Latin nōnāgintā, \"ninety\"."
            }
