              "text": "тысяча (týsyacha) from Proto-Slavic tysęti — inherited, a cousin of Lithuanian tūkstantis and Gothic þūsundi, \"thousand\" (Vasmer): English thousand is a cousin. One proposal Vasmer reports reads it as \"a swollen hundred\"."
